# __PROJECT_NAME__

A MoonBit game using Kagura's released Web runtime.

Requires Node.js 24+, pnpm, MoonBit, and a WebGPU browser. The Mooncakes
dependencies in `moon.mod` require the Kagura release containing the new layout.

```sh
pnpm install
kagura dev                  # http://127.0.0.1:8080
kagura build                # dist/
```

`pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, and the provided `justfile` also work without the CLI.
Move the green character with WASD or the arrow keys. Edit `main.mbt` to change
the game; the dev server rebuilds and reloads it automatically.

Publish the contents of `dist/` to a static HTTP host. Relative URLs support
subdirectory deployments. No Kagura checkout or local path dependency is needed.

`username/__PROJECT_NAME__` is the starter module name. When changing it, update
both `moon.mod` and the `mbt:` import in `web.mjs`.

The generated `runtime/` contains the matching browser host distribution
(Apache-2.0), not the engine's MoonBit source. Keep it with this project.
